The '''Qymish people''', or simply '''Qymish''', are the largest ethnic group native to [[Qym]]. Worldwide, approximately 200 million people are of Qymish descent, making them one of the largest ethnic groups. Qymish people represent 83.7% of the population in [[Qym]], TBD% of the population in [[NEIGHBOR]] and TBD% of the population in [[NEIGHBOR]]. 

Qymish people are considered to be the descendants of the [[Byrakans]] and the [[Sukats]], but also other tribes that inhabited the Qymish territories during the late antiquity period, such as the [[Ottelians]]. The history of the Qymish as an ethnic group began with the separation of [[Northern Sukatia]] from the [[Sukats Kingdom]], resulting in the formation of the [[Duchy of Qym]] in {{abbr|1100|914 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. 

==Exonyms==
The Qymish endonym ''Qymaja'' is derived from the Byrakan word ''Qiim'' giving the name to [[Qym]], meaning "land of squirrels". Due to the lack of Q or Y sounds in many languages, various exonyms were created to refer to [[Qym]] and its people. 

In [[Pamil language|Pamil]], Qymish people are known as ᨀᨎᨈᨙᨃᨖ ''Khîmu''. 

In [[Genonian language|Genonian]], Qymish people are known as 𐑙𐑰𐑥𐑪𐑯 ''Ĥîmân''.

